<title>JAPAN: Asahi Bank to issue Y100 bln in preferred shares.</title>
<headline>Asahi Bank to issue Y100 bln in preferred shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Asahi Bank Ltd said on Tuesday that it plans to issue 100 billion yen worth of preferred stock overseas.</p>
<p>The leading Japanese commercial bank said in a statement that the planned issue of 50 million preferred shares was designed to bolster its financial strength and make its business base more solid.  </p>
<p>The preferred shares will be priced at 2,000 each, and the payment date is August 7, the bank said in a statement.</p>
